Subject: [PATCH 13/13] Wait out a key cooldown when nothing else can answer

Reason: On 2026-11-07 a desktop task configured with only the free Nonoka
Cloud provider failed at 75% with "No API key for NONOKA_CLOUD could be
tried: 1 in a transient cooldown after recent errors". One upstream hiccup at
the relay had spent the key's three sticky retries (about 30 s of backoff),
the (tier, model, key) combo went into its 20-minute skip, and with no second
key and no second provider the next correction window had nothing to rotate
to: the chain raised, the window failed, the run failed. The cooldown is
persisted, so "继续" before the skip ended failed the same way.

Resumed, the same task failed twice more without a single skip. A
generation hung until its 10600 s hard deadline, the retry 5 s later hit a
45 s TLS handshake timeout, and the two counted as "consecutive timeouts" and
aborted the call; on the next resume two dropped handshakes aborted it in
under two minutes. The next morning the relay's upstream answered 522 until
the sticky retries ran out, and that raised straight through.

The skip window is 5 minutes instead of 20, and the sticky same-key retries
are 6 instead of 3 (5, 9, 17, 33, 65, 129 s of backoff, so a combo only
reaches the cooldown after about four minutes of failures). A connect timeout
neither counts toward the consecutive-timeout abort nor resets it: the abort
guards against sitting through a second hard deadline, which a 45 s handshake
says nothing about.

A failure is now `cooling` when it ends by itself: a
`ProviderUnavailableError` whose keys were all skipped for their cooldown (or
left to a sibling's probe), or the provider error itself when every key tried
spent its retries on a retryable error and so has just started cooling --
with no daily lock among the skips either way. `cooldown_until` is the
earliest skip end. The candidate loop marks its final exception with whether
*only* cooling failures stopped the chain, and `RoleClient.complete` (the old
body is now `_complete_routed`) waits such a chain out: it warns
`llm-cooldown-wait` with the time it will retry and the failure, sleeps until
the skip ends (30 s polls for a key left to a probe), and runs the chain
again, whose first call is the cooldown's probe. A chain that also failed some
other way, a permanent error, a daily lock, a missing key and two hard
deadlines in a row still raise at once; the waiting is capped at 60 minutes
per call.

The openai_compat transport also quotes a non-JSON body without its leading
whitespace: the relay's heartbeat is one space per 15 s, so past 50 minutes
its trailing "HTTP 502" marker fell out of the 200-character quote and the
failure read as a non-retryable HTTP 200.

Upstream's three retries guarded the Gemini free tiers' daily budget, which
the desktop does not use; the cloud image shares the engine but runs no LLM
stages.

Removal: Delete once upstream waits out cooldowns that leave the chain empty,
or the desktop stops shipping a single-key provider without a fallback.

